// TIME VORTEX — ORBITAL — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// TIME VORTEX as Berlin-school sequencer music. The walking bass becomes a 16th sequencer
// (same notes, octave-hopping), a second sequence plays a chord tone every three sixteenths
// (three against four, drifting across the bar lines), a Minimoog answers and harmonises, a
// synth choir, electric grand, gated snare, Simmons toms. Theremin, strings, vibes, pews and
// crash are Peter's, from gravity.js.
// 
//   1-4    intro: sequencer and sub, strings from bar 2, cross-sequence and kick from bar 3
//   5-12   A, half-time snare
//   13-20  A2 + choir, Minimoog fills at the phrase ends
//   21-28  BUILD (as gravity.js), Simmons tom fill
//   29-36  A3: Minimoog plays the A line under the theremin's A2, grand comping
//   37-44  ZERO-G: drums out but a heartbeat; the A melody on theremin, echoed a bar late
//          an octave down on electric grand
//   45-48  BUILD 2 (the build's last four bars), snare roll, riser
//   49-56  CLIMAX: theremin + grand octave + Minimoog harmony + choir, strings restruck, toms
//   57-60  WIND-DOWN: the second half of A at A's level
// 60 bars at 112; loops 5-60. Written by work/local/_vortex-remixes.mjs.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
